   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. The stereo marks for the wedged and hashed centres are my own geometric reading of the image. I did not check the CIP labels.\n\n**Left fragment**\n- The piperazine carries an N-carboxamide, N\u2013C(=O)NH2.\n- Its stereocentre bears a hashed CH2C\u2261N group.\n- Its other nitrogen is bonded to C4 of the pyrimidine.\n\n**Core**\n- The pyrimidine is fused to a tetrahydropyridine ring. That ring's nitrogen carries a 1-naphthyl group.\n- Pyrimidine C2 bears an O\u2013CH2 link to the N-methylpyrrolidine.\n\n**Linker**\n- The pyrrolidine C4\u2013O (wedged) connects through a triethylene-glycol chain: O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O.\n- The chain ends on a benzene ring.\n\n**Benzene ring**\n- The chain-bearing oxygen sits ortho to the CH2NH group.\n- A 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group sits para to the CH2NH group.\n\n**Right fragment (VHL-type ligand)**\n- The CH2NH is acylated by a 4-hydroxyproline carboxamide.\n- The proline nitrogen is acylated by CH(3-methylisoxazol-5-yl)\u2013CH(CH3)2.\n- I assigned the hydroxyproline and acyl-carbon stereo by analogy with the standard VH032 ligand rather than deriving it from the drawing.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)N1CCN(c2nc(OC[C@@H]3C[C@@H](OCCOCCOCCOc4cc(-c5scnc5C)ccc4CNC(=O)[C@@H]4C[C@@H](O)CN4C(=O)[C@@H](c4cc(C)no4)C(C)C)CN3C)nc3c2CCN(c2cccc4ccccc24)C3)C[C@@H]1CC#N"
